abstract: >-
  Ophamin is an empirical observatory wrapped around a substrate under test.
  It is built for Kimera-SWM but independent of it: the substrate plugs in
  through one adapter and a MockSubstrate makes the framework runnable
  without Kimera. The architecture is six wheels in two concentric triads —
  an outer triad for empirical observation (seeing / measuring / comparing)
  and an inner triad for engineering observation (instrumenting / auditing /
  reporting) — plus cross-cutting layers for per-primitive inspection and
  standard-format interop (SARIF / JUnit XML / MLflow / CycloneDX SBOM).
  Six scenarios across three experimentation tiers (scientific, engineering,
  philosophical) produce signed 9-section Empirical Proof Records with
  pre-registered falsifiable claims.
